    // ---- the test builtin -------------------------------------------------------------
    // There is no real filesystem behind a grammar run, so the file predicates answer from a
    // small MODEL of the standard paths every shell can rely on. Anything else is "absent".
    //
    // Why not a real stat(): a native binary could call it (bash-rt.c links libc), but the
    // other two engines cannot - the tag-script host running this half has no filesystem
    // API, and llvm.Run's libcExterns (abnf/llvmmap.go) only lists what the IR interpreter
    // implements EXACTLY, which a stat struct is not. A stat() in one engine of three would
    // be a designed-in halves divergence.
    //
    // The model, checked with bash 5.3.15 (`test OP PATH`):
    //     /dev/null /dev/zero /dev/tty        -e -r -w -c      (character devices)
    //     / /dev /usr /bin /usr/bin           -e -d -s -r -x
    //     anything else                       nothing
